# Project: Atelier

A free, browser-first art studio (formerly CreativePhotoEditor). One engine, two workspaces: **Photo** (layers, move/resize, blend, export — working today) and **Pixel** (sprites for games — later slices). Browser is the product; a desktop wrap comes later around the same core. Full design docs live in `atelier-cursor-package/` (PROJECT_BRAIN, DECISIONS, ARCHITECTURE, ROADMAP, TAXONOMY) — read those before large work.

## Stack overrides
- Framework: Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript strict.
- Rendering: PixiJS (WebGL) — imported ONLY inside `core/render`.
- UI state: Zustand (`state/`) mirrors the LayerGraph; the LayerGraph is the source of truth.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS. File I/O: JSZip for the project container (`.cpe` today; `.atelier` with the format bump).
- Deploy: Vercel (main → Production, dev → Preview). Repo: github.com/nathanokh1/Atelier.

## Conventions
- Every LayerGraph mutation goes through a Command (`core/commands`) — never mutate
  the graph directly from a React handler. Undo/redo is not optional.
- Use TAXONOMY.md terms exactly (Document, Layer, Command, Export vs Save, etc.).
- Keep the `core/` layer framework-agnostic (no React/Next imports) so it survives
  a future Tauri/mobile wrap.
- KISS. If a feature isn't in the current ROADMAP phase, it's out of scope.

## Notes
